From 5558fbeafeab351003b8b90006258b95a40af9b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:14:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kernel, bcmdrivers: privilege checks and memory-safety fixes
 (2026-11-03 review)

- bcm_knvram: the nvram netlink family answers only a sender with CAP_SYS_ADMIN (not
  CAP_NET_ADMIN, which the nobody dnsmasq keeps); message lengths are bounded by what arrived; the
  REGISTER name, the GETALL page index and the XFR string are bounded and terminated.
- proc_cmd.h: the /proc command consoles are owner-write; the command line is always terminated.
- blog.c: blog_drv_ioctl() requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN before it takes its lock.
- bcm_mcast: IGMP / MLD snooping control over netlink requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN.
- Five 4.19 stable backports: CVE-2023-42752 (igmpv3_newpack size cap), CVE-2024-36904
  (tcp_twsk_unique reference), CVE-2024-56631 (sg_release order), CVE-2024-41012
  (locks_remove_posix on the fcntl/close race), CVE-2024-47685 (zeroed IPv6 RST header).
- ipt_TRIGGER: the trigger lock is held from each lookup until the entry is used (the timer could
  free it in between); the flush frees only entries whose timer it cancelled, outside the lock; no
  conntrack entry, no DNAT.
- xt_webstr: per-CPU HTTP state; the data length runs from the TCP data to the end of the linear
  buffer (IPv4 and IPv6); the terminator scan is bounded before each read.
- dnsmq: the control writes copy the user buffer with copy_from_user().
- bcm_bca_usb_xhci: ubus_credits is accepted from 1 to 32 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
